    "updated_at": "2025-09-12T06:17:35Z",
    "body": "The RFCs are not that relevant for our decisions here, but I think you are misreading them. In particular RFC 8089 appears to require that any `file:` URL scheme is followed by either `/` or `//` in its syntax section.\n\nWe also very much don't want to grab a base URL from the environment. That it has to be provided explicitly is a design decision that we can't really revisit well over a decade in.",
